+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+- A client can request its conversation summaries with `list_conversations`; `limit`, when present, is an integer from 1 through 200, and `before`, when present, is the complete `{updatedAt, sessionId}` cursor from its last row ([validated by: validates the list request and its paging fields](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+- When `transport.history` is enabled, the server answers with one `conversation_list` whose summaries are newest first and whose dates are ISO strings; it takes the user id from the authenticated connection, never an extra field in the frame, and passes the optional paging values to the store unchanged ([validated by: answers with the authenticated user’s newest conversations and forwards the cursor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L110)).
+- When history is disabled, or the configured store cannot list conversations, the server answers with an `UNSUPPORTED` error rather than an empty list ([validated by: reports UNSUPPORTED when history is disabled or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L150)).
 
